arm64: dts: h713: GPU DVFS at stock's points, and a GPU thermal trip

The GPU had no operating points, so it ran flat out at one rate. Its
thermal zone had no trips, so nothing could throttle it. That was
harmless while the GPU sat idle. It is not harmless now that the GPU
does letterboxing, rotation, subtitles, and AV1 above 720p.

PLL_GPU is pinned at 600 MHz by assigned-clock-rates. The table is
600 MHz divided by the GPU clock's M divider (150/200/300/600), so a
DVFS step never relocks the PLL; see the preceding clk patch. Stock
holds PLL_GPU at exactly 600 MHz in every capture and lists these four
points for this die. Every point is 960 mV, the fixed vdd_sys, which is
the voltage stock gives every GPU point.

This raises the GPU's ceiling from 432 MHz to 600 MHz. The old 432 MHz
was an accident of reset defaults; clk_summary reported 864 MHz.

gpu-thermal gets a passive trip at 85 C, the same temperature as the
CPU's hot trip, and a critical trip at 105 C. It also gets a cooling map
onto the GPU's devfreq cooling device, which needs CONFIG_DEVFREQ_THERMAL.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -282,6 +282,41 @@
 		 */
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * GPU DVFS, frequency only. vdd_sys is fixed at 960 mV, the voltage
+	 * stock gives every GPU point. PLL_GPU is held at 600 MHz -- what the
+	 * vendor stack programs (0xb8001800 in every CCU capture) -- and the
+	 * points are 600 MHz / M, the GPU clock's own 2-bit divider, so DVFS
+	 * never relocks the PLL. They are the stock table's points for this
+	 * die; stock runs the top one with DVFS off.
+	 *
+	 * Before this table the GPU ran at 432 MHz, while clk_summary
+	 * claimed 864 (PLL_GPU's output divider was not modelled).
+	 */
+	gpu_opp_table: opp-table-gpu {
+		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
+
+		opp-150000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <150000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <960000>;
+		};
+
+		opp-200000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <200000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <960000>;
+		};
+
+		opp-300000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <300000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <960000>;
+		};
+
+		opp-600000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <600000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <960000>;
+		};
+	};
+
 	timer {
 		compatible = "arm,armv8-timer";
 		interrupts = <GIC_PPI 13 0xf08>,
@@ -402,9 +437,29 @@
 		};
 
 		gpu-thermal {
-			polling-delay-passive = <0>;
+			polling-delay-passive = <250>;
 			polling-delay = <1000>;
 			thermal-sensors = <&ths 1>;
+
+			trips {
+				gpu_hot: gpu-hot {
+					temperature = <85000>;
+					hysteresis = <2000>;
+					type = "passive";
+				};
+				gpu_crit: gpu-crit {
+					temperature = <105000>;
+					hysteresis = <5000>;
+					type = "critical";
+				};
+			};
+
+			cooling-maps {
+				map0 {
+					trip = <&gpu_hot>;
+					cooling-device = <&gpu THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
+				};
+			};
 		};
 	};
 
@@ -1413,6 +1468,9 @@
 			clock-names = "core", "bus";
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_GPU>;
 			mali-supply = <&reg_vdd_sys>;
+			assigned-clocks = <&ccu CLK_PLL_GPU>;
+			assigned-clock-rates = <600000000>;
+			operating-points-v2 = <&gpu_opp_table>;
 			/*
 			 * Power domain index 0 = GPU, per the stock DTB's pd_gpu@0.
 			 * The previous <&ppu 2> aimed at what stock calls TVCAP, and
